WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.280
Damn, Bruce...that's metal.

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:07.170
Footage from a camera test for The Batman
featuring Robert Pattinson in the Batsuit

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:11.059
has officially been unveiled, and fans are
already picking it apart.

00:00:11.059 --> 00:00:14.719
Among their more fascinating discoveries:
Batman's chest plate appears to have been

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:16.760
made from repurposed materials.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.119
Although the footage is bathed in red light,
it does reveal a pretty sweet-looking Batsuit

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:25.269
with a solemn Robert Pattinson demonstrating
that, at the very least, he has the right

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:26.410
jaw for the part.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:31.320
The chest plate really turned heads, though;
at first glance, it simply appears to be mechanical,

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.330
possibly made from a pair of Batarangs or
some other gadgets of the type that the Dark

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.610
Knight is inclined to utilize.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:44.490
At second glance, though, it looks like something
much more hardcore: pieces of a gun.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:45.780
"Bob?

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.070
Gun."

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.220
Now, we know what you may be thinking: Batman
doesn't use guns.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:52.620
Heck, he hates guns.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.680
Why on Earth would he have pieces of one embedded
in his costume?

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.770
Fans think they know the answer, and if you
haven't guessed it yet, prepare for a big

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:01.950
ol' explosion inside your cranium.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:05.840
The theory is that it isn't just any gun that
Batman may have used to construct his chest

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:06.840
plate.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.659
Fans believe that the possible gun in question
will serve to remind Bruce Wayne, every single

00:01:10.659 --> 00:01:15.049
time he goes to put on that suit, why he's
putting himself in danger to protect the citizens

00:01:15.049 --> 00:01:16.049
of Gotham.

00:01:16.049 --> 00:01:19.280
The gun that can prod him to think of the
innocent lives that might be lost if he should

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:23.970
lose his focus the gun that set him on the
path to becoming the Batman in the first place.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:28.170
That's right: the idea goes that protecting
Batman's heart in the new Batsuit could be

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:30.340
the gun that was used to kill his parents.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.939
Fans weren't the only ones to jump on this
possibility.

00:01:32.939 --> 00:01:37.119
Filmmaker and comic book writer Kevin Smith
was among the first to notice that the insignia

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:41.890
on the new Batman costume could be made from
a gun because if it's indeed true, he's likely

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:44.299
the one that gave the film's team the idea.

00:01:44.299 --> 00:01:48.840
Smith was among the many writers to participate
in the creation of Detective Comics #1000,

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:53.340
a 2019 tome that featured a plethora of intriguing
Batman tales.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:57.130
In Smith's story, Bruce Wayne melted down
the firearm that was used in his parents'

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:01.209
murder, fashioning it into a plate that was
hidden under the logo on his chest.

00:02:01.209 --> 00:02:03.630
If this is true, it could be a very savvy
move.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:08.060
The murder of Thomas and Martha Wayne is a
well-known and oft-depicted element of Batman's

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:12.400
story, and it'd be easy to make the case that
The Batman would do well to avoid revisiting

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.020
that particular plot point.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:17.980
Using their murder weapon as an element of
Batman's costume could serve as a compelling

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:22.210
visual signifier of the Dark Knight's origin
a way to ensure that even if they're never

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:27.000
even seen onscreen, the Waynes' presence will
loom large over The Batman's narrative.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.100
The gun that killed Batman's parents also
appears in an arguably even more significant

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:34.630
way in the pages of the wondrously loony Batman:
Year Two.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:38.670
At a tense point in the first issue's narrative,
Bruce Wayne decides that the proper way to

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:42.780
avenge his parents' deaths is to take the
gun involved in their murder and fire it at

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:43.780
someone else.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:47.730
Circling back to the new Batman costume, fans
have pointed out that it seems to be something

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:50.410
of an amalgam of a number of Batsuits past.

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:54.160
Among its more prominent features is a popped
collar, which calls to mind the design of

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:59.690
the cowl in Gotham by Gaslight, the 1989 comic
and later animated film that posited an alternate

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:02.370
version of Batman operating in the Victorian
era.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:05.170
"I need your files on the Ripper."

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:09.310
The shoulder pieces and overall aesthetic
of the new Batsuit also seem to owe a lot

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:15.040
to Batman's design in the Arkham video game
series particularly 2015's Arkham Knight while

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:19.370
the mask is reminiscent of nothing so much
as the classic design from Tim Burton's original

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:21.170
1989 flick Batman.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:25.870
If the Batman team was going for a best-of-all-worlds
kind of feel with the new Batsuit, then so

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.920
far, it's looking like they pretty much nailed
it.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:32.220
The Batman is scheduled for release on June
25, 2021.

